# The coordination board is append-only: every session adds its block at the end, so every
# merge used to stop on a conflict in this one file, and twice the conflict markers were
# committed to main. Git's built-in "union" driver resolves that case by keeping the lines
# from both sides. It applies to this file only. Generated pages must never use it: rebuild
# them with their generator instead.
COORDINATION.md merge=union
